        "session_id": "5096da06-04f7-4b7d-894b-30084fc499fc",
        "position": 2,
        "content": "Почему обработчик ThreadPerTaskWebServer должен быть потокобезопасным?",
        "answer": "Обработчик задач должен быть потокобезопасным, так как код обработки задач может вызываться одновременно для нескольких задач. [DOC:structure-0008]\nПодход с одним потоком на задачу обеспечивает лучшую отзывчивость и пропускную способность, позволяя обрабатывать несколько запросов параллельно. [DOC:structure-0007] [DOC:structure-0008]",
        "status": "done",
        "kind": "question",
        "question_scope": "document",
        "search_question": "Why must the ThreadPerTaskWebServer request handler be thread-safe?",
        "sources": [
          {
            "kind": "document",
            "chunk_id": "structure-0008",
            "source": "https://jcip.net/jcip-sample.pdf",
            "title": "Java Concurrency in Practice — sample chapter",
            "section": "6.1.2 Explicitly creating threads for tasks",
            "page_start": 3,
            "page_end": 3
          },
          {
            "kind": "document",
            "chunk_id": "structure-0007",
            "source": "https://jcip.net/jcip-sample.pdf",
            "title": "Java Concurrency in Practice — sample chapter",
            "section": "6.1.2 Explicitly creating threads for tasks",
            "page_start": 3,
            "page_end": 3
          }
        ],
        "citations": [
          {
            "chunk_id": "structure-0008",
            "quote": " Task-handling code must be thread-safe, because it may be invoked concur- rently for multiple tasks."
          },
          {
            "chunk_id": "structure-0007",
            "quote": "This enables new connections to be accepted before previous requests complete, improving responsiveness."
          },
          {
            "chunk_id": "structure-0008",
            "quote": "As long as the request arrival rate does not exceed the ser ver ’s capacity to handle requests, this approach offers better responsiveness and throughput."
          }
        ],
